0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}Ax.\n$$\n\nFor a symmetric matrix $A$, the gradient of the function $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax$ with respect to $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=2Ax.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $A$ is symmetric, we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532650 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fe0d364-ef22-5138-9ee5-e473bd909447" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradient of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f851010-ea30-50ca-aace-f98e8eb2ec46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532066} {:answer/id #uuid "7b865f86-0d16-5302-9cc6-a10c9f8f37ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532209} {:answer/id #uuid "c32739f0-0d80-5ef2-8e02-dfabb53b4363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532350} {:answer/id #uuid "d42e932d-9ed9-55f9-b7a7-ebf31d9b817a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532388} {:answer/id #uuid "ecefcf4c-8447-5494-8e2d-cad863dd1b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c32739f0-0d80-5ef2-8e02-dfabb53b4363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532350} :answer-field/id #uuid "c117a905-5939-59e0-9a30-20c1c80001bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "45fa10fd-570c-5dfa-b523-d7d0d1d7035b" :question/math-academy-id "q-265769" :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]x\n$$\n\n with respect to $x$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Writing $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}Ax.\n$$\n\nFor a symmetric matrix $A$, the gradient of the function $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax$ with respect to $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=2Ax.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $A$ is symmetric, we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=2[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c77271f-3d21-5193-a1ad-5c0264e337f0" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule to Gradients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01c3cde9-216b-5b06-a2d7-f17bcc359a07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531937} {:answer/id #uuid "952049ad-9e8a-5b7c-8a40-1b529b790b30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532273} {:answer/id #uuid "c8e551dd-aff9-5cdf-a21e-dee3bfc6a1df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532366} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d16db9-d28a-5208-8418-ea2e4224aad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 32 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532414} {:answer/id #uuid "eedfdf30-92c3-5e54-aaf9-5fb07ffd1c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 32 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eedfdf30-92c3-5e54-aaf9-5fb07ffd1c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 32 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532449} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ac8dc5d-b24d-5234-9c6b-196229d7d8cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186205335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa5725de-7db0-574b-a1ac-d3be9e0fac87" :question/math-academy-id "q-269389" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=2(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b.$ Then, $L(x)=2{y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{T}y)=4{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(Ax-b)=A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 4y \\\\  & =4\\cdot {A}^{T}(Ax-b) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}([\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 32 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c77271f-3d21-5193-a1ad-5c0264e337f0" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule to Gradients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42dd4b42-211d-5972-b5c4-cf90c5e8012b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}120 & 0 & 180\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532073} {:answer/id #uuid "957a9f6c-3b1e-5704-941b-815bbeb74ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 120 \\\\ 180\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532274} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d6caca-dd94-5d02-ac30-3a83b5799cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 & 12 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532330} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3252ab-ce3d-5f5e-9724-067f5f2fb76b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532369} {:answer/id #uuid "de485c91-3834-59a5-9cbb-f1af63ef0211" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "957a9f6c-3b1e-5704-941b-815bbeb74ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 120 \\\\ 180\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532274} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bbd1a5c-0501-5482-a310-9debd05ca9bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5a5695b-8296-5985-af65-b20134a9d8cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-269465" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=(5Ax-b)^{T}(5Ax-b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=5Ax-b.$ Then, $L(x)={y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{T}y)=2{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5Ax-b)=5A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & =(5A)^{T}\\cdot 2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & =(5A)^{T}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =10\\cdot {A}^{T}(5Ax-b) \\\\  & =10\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}(5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}](5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =10\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 120 \\\\ 180\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c77271f-3d21-5193-a1ad-5c0264e337f0" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule to Gradients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "142f877f-e698-5254-93da-53589da88451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531972} {:answer/id #uuid "3b802d7a-2645-5ba2-9341-530841a24204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -10 & 30\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532058} {:answer/id #uuid "733ac048-f58d-5680-814f-d36675d8c2f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532194} {:answer/id #uuid "9d2f0e60-7b67-503d-9ec7-438462275ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532292} {:answer/id #uuid "f414dbbc-4b36-56b2-8d02-f57f2d9a1e36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "142f877f-e698-5254-93da-53589da88451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531972} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d61f281-b20f-5b2b-9b40-f631fe100b4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "411aabaa-bd7a-5b74-b0d5-19adca16cb89" :question/math-academy-id "q-269470" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=(Ax-2b)^{T}(Ax-2b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=Ax-2b.$ Then, $L(x)={y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{T}y)=2{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(Ax-2b)=A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =2\\cdot {A}^{T}(Ax-2b) \\\\  & =2\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c77271f-3d21-5193-a1ad-5c0264e337f0" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule to Gradients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65b8247f-5cca-5ad6-b7e6-1c0348949372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 34\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532159} {:answer/id #uuid "97adc8aa-27be-581c-8f16-71be62025db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532279} {:answer/id #uuid "a3fd209b-0c16-51c1-a53b-64513496bb0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532303} {:answer/id #uuid "b5373f73-c69f-5551-8e02-a40eab04c3e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-68 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532332} {:answer/id #uuid "c5783d90-4abf-5066-b1d9-6d183ea64767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 49\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5373f73-c69f-5551-8e02-a40eab04c3e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-68 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532332} :answer-field/id #uuid "2057498e-fa7c-5977-b9d8-e7c0c6099eb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532506}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c92e05a7-340f-573b-9fe1-3137e228de5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-269518" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=2(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b.$ Then, $L(x)=2{y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{T}y)=4{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(Ax-b)=A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={A}^{T}\\cdot 4y \\\\  & =4\\cdot {A}^{T}(Ax-b) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}([\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 16 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-68 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c77271f-3d21-5193-a1ad-5c0264e337f0" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule to Gradients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4182ba73-9501-5f1c-9045-cd1a7928503c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-35 & 55\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532068} {:answer/id #uuid "53197217-2f27-584f-b12c-4e35c041f0cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532112} {:answer/id #uuid "679dcc5a-5a9f-55d5-aac6-b3a5f41d78af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}17 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532164} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-24 \\\\ -68\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532173} {:answer/id #uuid "c6597316-83c7-5e8b-81d5-baa98c470d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}49 & -32\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a9dc4e7-8077-518c-b53a-ff8f2d256e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-24 \\\\ -68\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532173} :answer-field/id #uuid "86232881-3656-545b-b963-9a0c99bf87aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41cc5d66-bf23-517e-b32a-3cd7a74b1b32" :question/math-academy-id "q-269549" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by $L(x)=(2Ax+b)^{T}(2Ax+b)$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{x}L(x)$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this problem by applying the chain rule for gradients.\n\nLet $y=2Ax+b.$ Then, $L(x)={y}^{T}y,$ and\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}L={(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{T}y)=2{y}^{T}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2Ax+b)=2A,\n$$\n\nwe have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{T}\\cdot {(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}y})}^{T} \\\\  & =(2A)^{T}\\cdot 2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}L & =(2A)^{T}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =4\\cdot {A}^{T}(2Ax+b) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}(2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}](2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 \\\\ -68\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2198cf08-3a99-5e5d-80af-bbe722b51647" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradient of a Quadratic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b276ba5e-614d-56eb-b840-b87c5c18abf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532328} :answer-field/id #uuid "82d0d7d4-31f3-54e7-86b5-9d1ef86a79fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186205485} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "785c6b67-1726-563e-bd72-64447433e923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532202} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca8ad3b1-ab23-5b80-9e34-bf9e8ced4f6b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186205486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d373e229-cbc5-5c4a-acf6-948959b19522" :question/math-academy-id "q-276039" :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x\n$$\n\nwith respect to $x$ at  $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}.$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">$\\,{∇}_{x}f=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Defining the matrix $A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe have $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax.$\n\nSince $A$ is not symmetric, we use the more general formula for the gradient of a quadratic function:\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=({A}^{T}+A)x\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}+A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, compute the gradient at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f(x) & =({A}^{T}+A)x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+0 \\\\ 3+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532660 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2198cf08-3a99-5e5d-80af-bbe722b51647" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradient of a Quadratic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2f41369-88fc-57d9-9f6c-32363ff7bcbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answe