$A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe have $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax.$\n\nSince $A$ is not symmetric, we use the more general formula for the gradient of a quadratic function:\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=({A}^{T}+A)x\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}+A & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, compute the gradient at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f(x) & =({A}^{T}+A)x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4-3 \\\\ 3+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2198cf08-3a99-5e5d-80af-bbe722b51647" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradient of a Quadratic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4ef699f-857f-5b56-9ba4-64e4abbc9940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532465} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b288cd4-9ea2-5bcc-bf0a-296457d3c81e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532533} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85ce4622-61e3-5161-8887-f7653a676c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532236} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa55b97d-8499-5057-8619-61c35e2dc5f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9de18b18-ac36-55ed-9eeb-ad23a6b9ac98" :question/math-academy-id "q-276042" :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]x\n$$\n\nwith respect to $x$ at  $x={[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}.$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">$\\,{∇}_{x}f=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Defining the matrix $A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe have $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax.$\n\nSince $A$ is not symmetric, we use the more general formula for the gradient of a quadratic function:\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=({A}^{T}+A)x\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}+A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, compute the gradient at $x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f(x) & =({A}^{T}+A)x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0+0 \\\\ 0+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2198cf08-3a99-5e5d-80af-bbe722b51647" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradient of a Quadratic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "227e2fbf-1d08-52e2-8bba-7c210918adda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "227e2fbf-1d08-52e2-8bba-7c210918adda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532006} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e2ac6c8-308e-5ccb-b6d7-b77764401e1c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9a795b8-272f-565d-b750-ab45ec83143c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9a795b8-272f-565d-b750-ab45ec83143c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532316} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a3d4772-d0cb-5d4d-8e1f-b23b20b49b43" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a1a89719-12d3-55da-8498-af0dfd930411" :question/math-academy-id "q-276045" :question/problem "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x\n$$\n\nwith respect to $x$ at  $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}.$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"30px\">$\\,{∇}_{x}f=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Defining the matrix $A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe have $f(x)={x}^{T}Ax.$\n\nSince $A$ is not symmetric, we use the more general formula for the gradient of a quadratic function:\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=({A}^{T}+A)x\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}+A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, compute the gradient at $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x}f(x) & =({A}^{T}+A)x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6-8 \\\\ -4+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186208847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2198cf08-3a99-5e5d-80af-bbe722b51647" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Gradient of a Quadratic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05c026ae-ac1c-53eb-98c4-1750389eab42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math